'''Fred Tatasciore''' {{born|13|June|1968}} is a voice actor who voiced [[Lieutenant]] [[Shaxs]] on {{s|LD}}. 

He also voiced other characters on ''Lower Decks'' and {{s|PRO}}. Earlier, he lent his voice to {{film|12}}. Together with [[David Sobolov]] he provided all the [[Klingon 23rd patrol 002|Klingon voices]] heard in the film except the one of [[Sean Blakemore]]. Sobolov and Tatasciore were coached by [[Marc Okrand]].

Tatasciore is known to be the voice of the {{w|Hulk (comics)|Hulk}}, the {{w|Beast (comics)|Beast}}, and {{w|Bane (comics)|Bane}} in several animated films and series and video games. He voiced [[James T. Kirk]], [[Leonard McCoy]], and [[Spock]] in several episodes of the television series ''[[Robot Chicken]]'' (2005-14).

Tatasciore attended the UCLA and started as voice actor in the early 1980s when he worked on the English dubbed versions of the Hong Kong action films ''Dragon Lord'' (1982), {{wt|roject A (film)|Project A}} (1983), {{wt|Born to Defence}} (1986), ''Swordsman II'' (1992), ''The Bodyguard from Beijing'' (1994), ''Fist of Legend'' (1994), and ''High Risk'' (1995).

Further film work includes {{wt|Team America: World Police}} (2004), {{wt|Final Fantasy VII: Advent Children}} (2005), {{wt|The Wild}} (2006, [[William Shatner]], [[Richard Kind]], [[Greg Cipes]], [[David Cowgill]], [[Kevin Michael Richardson]], [[Nicholas Guest]], [[Nolan North]] and [[Julianne Buescher]]), and {{wt|The Ant Bully (film)|The Ant Bully}} (2006), {{wt|Charlotte's Web (2006 film)|Charlotte's Web}} (2006), {{wt|Dead Silence}} (2007, with [[Bob Gunton]]), {{wt|TMNT (film)|TMNT}} (2007, with [[Patrick Stewart]], Nolan North, Kevin Michael Richardson, and [[Barbara Harris]]), ''Meet the Robinsons'' (2007), {{wt|Enchanted (film)|Enchanted}} (2007), {{wt|Beowulf (2007 film)|Beowulf}} (2007, with [[Sharisse Baker-Bernard]], [[Greg Ellis]], [[Shay Duffin]], and [[Dominic Keating]]), {{wt|Madagascar: Escape 2 Africa}} (2008), {{wt|9 (2009 animated film)|9}} (2009), ''The Princess and the Frog'' (2009), and ''Tangled'' (2010, with [[Donna Murphy]]), {{wt|Hellraiser: Revelations}} (2011), and {{wt|Kung Fu Panda 2}} (2011), {{wt|Wreck-It Ralph}} (2012), ''Planes'' (2013), {{wt|Frozen (2013 film)|Frozen}} (2013), and ''Planes: Fire & Rescue'' (2014).

On television, Tatasciore lent his voice to the series ''Naruto'' (2002-03), {{wt|Star Wars: Clone Wars (2003 TV series)|Star Wars: Clone Wars}} (2005), {{wt|What's New, Scooby-Doo?}} (2003-05), {{wt|Invader Zim}} (2001-06), {{wt|Tim and Eric Awesome Show, Great Job!}} (2007), {{wt|Grim & Evil}} (2005-07), {{wt|Ben 10 (2005 TV series)|Ben 10}} (2006-08), ''Naruto: Shippûden'' (2007-08), {{wt|Wolverine and the X-Men (TV series)|Wolverine and the X-Men}} (2008-09, with Nolan North and [[Susan Dalian]]), ''Back at the Barnyard'' (2007-09), ''Wolverine'' (2011), ''The Cleveland Show'' (2009-11, with Kevin Michael Richardson), ''X-Men'' (2011, with [[Cam Clarke]]), {{wt|Batman: The Brave and the Bold}} (2010-11, starring [[Diedrich Bader]]), {{wt|The Penguins of Madagascar}} (2010-12), {{wt|ThunderCats (2011 TV series)|ThunderCats}} (2012), ''The Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes'' (2010-12), {{wt|Tron: Uprising}} (2012), ''Scooby-Doo! Mystery Incorporated'' (2010-13, with [[Frank Welker]]), {{wt|Mad (TV series)|Mad}} (2010-13), ''Kung Fu Panda: Legends of Awesomeness'' (2011-14), {{wt|Monsters vs. Aliens (TV series)|Monsters vs. Aliens}} (2013-14), {{wt|Mickey Mouse (TV series)|Mickey Mouse}} (2013-14), {{wt|Ultimate Spider-Man (TV series)|Ultimate Spider-Man}} (2012-15), ''American Dad'' (2005-15), ''[[Family Guy]]'' (1999-2015), ''Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles'' (2013-15), ''Marvel's Avengers Assemble'' (2013-15), and {{wt|Hulk and the Agents of S.M.A.S.H.}} (2013-15, with [[Clancy Brown]]).

Between 2012 and 2015, Tatasciore received five Behind the Voice Actors Awards nominations including a nomination as Voice Actor of the Year in 2014. {{imdb|name/nm0851317/awards}} In 2023, he voiced Lord Zedd in ''Power Rangers Cosmic Fury''.

He also lent his voice to over 250 video games such as ''X-Men: Next Dimension'' (2002), {{wt|Terminator 3: Rise of the Machines (video game)|Terminator 3: Rise of the Machines}} (2003), ''Metal Gear Solid 3: Snake Eater'' (2004), ''The SpongeBob SquarePants Movie'' (2004), ''The Lord of the Rings: The Battle for Middle-earth'' (2004), {{wt|Batman Begins (video game)|Batman Begins}} (2005), {{wt|The Matrix: Path of Neo}} (2005), {{wt|Age of Empires III}} (2005), {{wt|Marvel: Ultimate Alliance}} (2006), ''World of Warcraft: The Burning Crusade'' (2007), {{wt|300: March to Glory}} (2007), {{wt|Transformers: The Game}} (2007), {{wt|BioShock}} (2007), {{wt|Halo 3}} (2007), {{wt|Assassin's Creed (video game)|Assassin's Creed}} (2007), {{wt|Uncharted: Drake's Fortune}} (2007), {{wt|Kung Fu Panda (video game)|Kung Fu Panda}} (2008), {{wt|The Incredible Hulk (2008 video game)|The Incredible Hulk}} (2008), ''007: Quantum of Solace'' (2008), {{wt|Call of Duty: World at War}} (2008), {{wt|X-Men Origins: Wolverine (video game)|X-Men Origins: Wolverine}} (2009), ''Transformers: Revenge of the Fallen'' (2009), {{wt|Batman: Arkham Asylum}} (2009), {{wt|Assassin's Creed II}} (2009), {{wt|Uncharted 2: Among Thieves}} (2009), {{wt|Mass Effect 2}} (2010), {{wt|Star Wars: The Force Unleashed II}} (2010), {{wt|Call of Duty: Black Ops}} (2010), {{wt|X-Men: Destiny}} (2011), {{wt|Uncharted 3: Drake's Deception}} (2011), {{wt|Star Wars: The Old Republic'}} (2011), {{wt|Diablo III}} (2012), {{wt|Halo 4}} (2012), {{wt|Resident Evil 6}} (2012), ''World of Warcraft: Mists of Pandaria'' (2012), {{wt|Deadpool (video game)|Deadpool}} (2013), ''Lego Marvel Super Heroes'' (2013), {{wt|Diablo III: Reaper of Souls}} (2014), {{wt|The Sims 4}} (2014), ''Call of Duty: Advanced Warfare'' (2014), and {{wt|Mortal Kombat X}} (2015).

